WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.416 --> 00:00:02.870
- When I'm night surfing the first thing

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:05.110
I really realize is how alone you are,

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.597
and how quiet everything is.

00:00:07.597 --> 00:00:10.980
It's the most free, spiritual
thing you could think of.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.470
But, once when you get
a wave it's incredible

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.141
just to see the colors come
off the waves off the board.

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:18.410
Every time I look down
when I'm night surfing

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.784
and I see that lit up board
I go, my dad created this.

00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:22.533
This is me and my dad.

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:25.986
(calm music)

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.330
My name is Sean Johnson.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.410
I'm a surfer and a surf coach
out of L.A. and I started

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.710
surfing because of my dad.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.090
My dad would take me out, he'd be surfing

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.650
and I'd be boogie boarding
in the white water.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:42.900
One day he's like, “Do you want to jump on?”

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.250
And I'm like, “Yeah, let's go.”

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.020
Threw me on the nose of his
surfboard and caught some waves

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.017
and I was like, “Dad, I want to do this.”

00:00:49.017 --> 00:00:51.097
So we'd be leaving the
beach and all of a sudden

00:00:51.097 --> 00:00:52.780
he'd be like, “Hey, look at
that board in the trash can.”

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.480
And I'd be like, “Yeah, look at
that board in the trash can.”

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.380
And he goes “No, that's your new board.”

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.225
- I would get boards out
of the trash at Malibu.

00:01:03.225 --> 00:01:06.240
Bring him home, strip all
the fiberglass off of them.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.156
Get in there, reshape the whole board

00:01:08.156 --> 00:01:10.490
the way I thought Sean
would like to ride it.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.360
He would get out there and
test my prototypes and say,

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.550
“You know, I really don't like this one

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.030
“or this one's great.”

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.950
Kind of sucks for me that
I don't surf anymore.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.600
But at the same time when
I'm shaping these boards,

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.933
I feel like I'm surfing.

00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:22.766
- [Sean] He does it all by hand.

00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:26.500
And that's the part that makes
me enjoy surfing them so much

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.160
cause I know how much
love and how much heart

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.410
is put into these boards.

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:37.140
(dramatic music)

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.230
- [Roy] In L.A. the
surfing is really crowded,

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:41.480
and I always thought that it
would be great to surf at night,

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.550
but it's kind of scary
out there at the night.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:46.120
I figured why not put some LEDs in a board

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.710
to where you can just get out there

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:51.090
and surf as long as you
want without the crowds.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.790
- As far as I know, my dad is the only one

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:55.203
making LED surfboards
in the United States.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.805
Maybe once a month when
there's a full moon

00:01:57.805 --> 00:01:59.030
we go night surfing.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.952
We cruise down to the beach,

00:02:00.952 --> 00:02:03.020
and it's just like old
times when we'd go surfing

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.650
but now we're sharing that night time

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.424
and he gets to enjoy me
surfing something he created.

00:02:07.424 --> 00:02:10.353
And I get to enjoy
riding something he made.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.800
Game time, boys.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.300
- [Roy] The best thing
about night surfing is

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.870
you get out there, it's quiet,
and it's kind of mysterious.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.670
- [Sean] My biggest fear is maybe falling,

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.320
knocking my head and getting knocked out

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.070
and no one being able to find me.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.880
So the cool part with having
those LED light boards

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.293
attached to you, you kind of
always be found or spotted.

00:02:30.407 --> 00:02:32.824
(slow music)

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.700
I think people are absolutely amazed

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.693
when they see the light
boards at night time.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.730
What are these flying light things

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.880
in the ocean right now?

00:02:44.504 --> 00:02:47.420
I feel like I'm an alien freakin' flying

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.633
on a huge space ship.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.230
- [Roy] Well surfing's really
a bond between Sean and I.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.610
I mean, you know, it's just so much fun

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.900
watching him out there surf.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.250
You know, now that I can't be out there

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.660
with him surfing, to see
him out there in the water,

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.840
tearing these boards up, you know,

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.070
it makes you feel really really proud.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.560
- [Sean] If I couldn't
surf, let alone surf

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.460
on my dad's surfboards, I
don't know what I would do.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.310
It reminds me of why I fell
in love with surfing so much.

